<title>POLAND: Kable extends gains on investor plans.</title>
<headline>Kable extends gains on investor plans.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish cable maker Kable SA jumped 6.4 percent to 30.1 zlotys, extending Monday's gain on news that Denmark's NKT Cables plans to increase its stake in the firm to over 50 percent, traders said.</p>
<p>Turnover amounted to 3.9 million zlotys.</p>
<p>&quot;The growth seems to be caused by the news that NKT Cables wants to increase its stake in Kable,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>But analysts said the stock was unlikely to rise again and should stabilise or fall in profit-taking in the next sessions.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
